    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "Find the derivative f’(x). Set the derivative equal to zero and solve for x. These x-values are the locations of the stationary points. Plug these x-values back into the original function f(x) to find the y-values. These (x, y) pairs are the stationary points. You can also use the second derivative to classify them as maxima, minima, or points of inflection.",
